# Skill: Content Provenance and Sol.site Binding

Use when wiring milling, noding, or transaction-pool agents to Transition Insight.

## Endpoints

- `/.well-known/provenance.json` — canonical URL, SNS, Sol.site alias, pool metadata
- `/attestation.json` — SHA-256 manifest of published ontology files (global tier)
- `/auth.md` — human-readable provenance notes for agents

## Identity chain

1. **Canonical:** `https://transition-insight.com`
2. **SNS:** `transition-insight.sol` (wallet-owned on Solana)
3. **Sol.site:** `https://transition-insight.sol.sites` (SNS → DNS gateway)
4. **DID:** `did:pkh:solana:<wallet>` from provenance / page meta (`author-did`)

Agents should treat the signed `manifestDigest` in attestation as the corpus
root hash for any slice-of-pool work. Per-file `sha256` entries identify individual essays.

## Sovereign publish (IPFS / IPNS via Pinata)

No GitHub, no Cloudflare origin. Build global tier, pin `out/`, publish IPNS:

```
cp .env.sovereign.example .env.local   # add PINATA_JWT, gateway, IPNS name
npm run deploy:sovereign
```

After first pin, set `NEXT_PUBLIC_IPFS_CID`, `NEXT_PUBLIC_IPFS_GATEWAY`, and
`NEXT_PUBLIC_IPNS_NAME` in `.env.local`, rebuild, and redeploy so
`provenance.json` and attestation reference the live CID.

Wire `transition-insight.com` via Pinata dedicated-gateway custom domain
(CNAME) or DNSLink (`_dnslink` TXT → `/ipns/<name>`). Sol.site can CNAME to
the same hostname once it resolves.

Until a CID is baked in, `provenance.json` reports `solSite.status: pending-dns`.

## Sign attestation (maintainer)

```
npm run content:attest
SOLANA_SIGNING_KEY=<base58-secret> npm run content:sign
npm run content:verify
```

Never commit `SOLANA_SIGNING_KEY`. Use the wallet that owns `transition-insight.sol`.

## Future milling / noding

When building transaction-pool or content-milling features:

- Verify attestation signature before indexing a corpus snapshot
- Bind on-chain program IDs to `manifestDigest` for decisive provenance
- Prefer `the-transaction.md` (Peridot / governance) as design context for rails
